ould, then we need to ignore extra? But problem says allocate exact budget, so maybe inputs are guaranteed that sum minima <= budget <= sum capacities. We'll assume that's the case.\n5. Construct allocations list in original segment order. Compute by_name dict. total = budget.\n\nReturn dict with allocations, by_name, total.\n\nEdge: the schema says by_name dynamicKeysFrom case.segments[*].name, so we must use exactly the names. No numeric validation.\n\nImplementation: use Python standard library. No mutation of case.\n\nWrite solve function accordingly.\n\nNow produce output JSON with implementation key and source code as string."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1250,"completion_tokens":1000,"total_tokens":2250,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":541},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":98},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}